From 141e03db7498e0c50dc035d2005a76685863875e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nova <361320585+q2-nova@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 11:23:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] mtd: spinand: add vendor-derived Dosilicon DS35Q2GA
 geometry

Add the E5/72 device used by the Q2 emulator: 2048+64-byte pages,
64 pages per eraseblock, 2048 blocks and two planes selected with column
bit 12. Reuse the DS35Q1GA OOB layout and standard four-bit ECC status.

The stock V1.32 dosilicon_param record at 0x80b30bd0 confirms page/block/
OOB/flash sizes, plane selection, ECC strength and quad mode. This agrees
with the SDK ingenic_sfc_v2/nand_device/dosilicon_nand.c at DiamondBond
revision 655f42c032402719881ff2a1b801bd797dc514c1.

The maximum factory bad-block count is absent from this evidence. Leave
it unspecified (zero, causing max_bad_blocks to return -ENOTSUPP) rather
than inventing a device guarantee. Bad-block/ECC injection and physical
OOB validation remain untested. Emulator erase/program/readback passes
across consecutive blocks on both planes.
---
 drivers/mtd/nand/spi/dosilicon.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/dosilicon.c b/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/dosilicon.c
index f99899866..54d270d15 100644
--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/dosilicon.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/dosilicon.c
@@ -68,6 +68,16 @@ static const struct spinand_info dosilicon_spinand_table[] = {
 					 &update_cache_variants),
 		SPINAND_HAS_QE_BIT,
 		SPINAND_ECCINFO(&ds35xx_ooblayout, NULL)),
+	SPINAND_INFO("DS35Q2GA",
+		SPINAND_ID(SPINAND_READID_METHOD_OPCODE_DUMMY, 0x72),
+		/* Vendor geometry; maximum factory bad-block count is unknown. */
+		NAND_MEMORG(1, 2048, 64, 64, 2048, 0, 2, 1, 1),
+		NAND_ECCREQ(4, 512),
+		SPINAND_INFO_OP_VARIANTS(&read_cache_variants,
+					 &write_cache_variants,
+					 &update_cache_variants),
+		SPINAND_HAS_QE_BIT,
+		SPINAND_ECCINFO(&ds35xx_ooblayout, NULL)),
 	SPINAND_INFO("DS35M1GA",
 		SPINAND_ID(SPINAND_READID_METHOD_OPCODE_DUMMY, 0x21),
 		NAND_MEMORG(1, 2048, 64, 64, 1024, 20, 1, 1, 1),
